        "identifier": "https://github.com/zblore/csd-lean4/blob/0d713bee53c64d6f07f7735c2203c6bf1d078e0d/CsdLean4/Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Projectivization/WignerRigidity.lean",
        "note": "My larger Lean project, where this proof was written. The theorem wigner_rigidity was first proved there on 2 July 2026 (commit c26c0954), the phase lemmas behind uniqueness followed on 7 July (683c3476), and uniqueness up to a phase on 6 August (097f9197). This repository copies the eleven files of its import closure from commit 0d713bee with the code unchanged and the comments edited. csd-lean4 at that commit uses Lean v4.34.0; the copied code builds unchanged on this repository's toolchain. New here: WignerLean/Basic.lean (the six Challenge statements and the antiunitary uniqueness in matrix form) and the controls.",
        "relationship": "builds-on"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/Bobart0/quantum-foundations-lean/blob/d632c676770890dc95f45aefa57d3d8655084a0c/QuantumFoundations/Wigner/Main.lean",
        "note": "QuantumFoundations, a Lean library (Apache-2.0). Its theorem wigner, first completed on 13 July 2026 (commit 44ce7f7a), proves Wigner's theorem for maps on the vectors of C^n that preserve |<x, y>| on unit vectors: such a map agrees, up to a phase on each unit vector, with a unitary or an antiunitary, without assuming bijectivity. Its Uniqueness.lean proves that the two cases exclude each other when n >= 2. Linked at the v1.4.3 snapshot, dated 21 September 2026. Read, not compiled.",
        "relationship": "independent"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/rwst/AoP-lean/blob/fcbf63eaf12482c0c8ac44e8a326e0d41cd75521/ForPhyslib/QuantumMechanics/Wigner/Theorem.lean",
        "note": "QuantumMechanics.Wigner, by Ralf Stephan (CC0), at a snapshot dated 31 October 2026. Read, not compiled. Its existence theorem is stronger than wigner here: for a complex Hilbert space of any dimension, a map on vectors that preserves |<v, w>| on unit vectors agrees, up to a phase on each unit vector, with a linear or conjugate-linear isometry, which is a unitary or an antiunitary when every ray is reached (automatic in finite dimension). Its uniqueness theorems assume finite dimension; wigner_unique here does not. It follows Gy. P. Geher's 2014 proof.",
        "relationship": "independent"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://palomar-registry.org/entry?id=PALOMAR-2026-08-21-000001&version=1",
        "note": "The real case of the theorem, WignerReal.exists_isometry_of_transProbPreserving, by Bryan Ehrlich (ehrlich-b/sequential-products-lean at 3c0e870e): a transition-probability-preserving map on the rays of a finite-dimensional real inner product space is induced by a linear isometry. A separate proof, written after the author vendored this proof's csd-lean4 file.",
        "relationship": "other"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/ehrlich-b/sequential-products-lean/blob/2751a8d9500a370dec971416b07f79707b2fc8bb/RadicalRelativity/Vendor/Wigner/WignerRigidity.lean",
        "note": "A copy of this proof's csd-lean4 file, vendored in August 2026 with my copyright and the statements unchanged. Not an independent proof.",
        "relationship": "other"
      },
